==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*līþaną}}. Sense developed from 'go, travel' to 'endure', then to 'suffer'.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlaɪ̯dn̩/|/ˈlaɪ̯dən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-leiden.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=1|leidet|litt|gelitten|past subjunctive=litte}}

# {{label|de|transitive}} to [[bear]]; to [[endure]]; to [[undergo]] (some hardship)
# {{label|de|intransitive}} to [[suffer]]; to feel [[pain]]
# {{label|de|intransitive}} to [[suffer]] (from; a disease)
#* '''2012''' April 20, ''{{w|Die Welt}}'' [http://epaper.apps.welt.de/welt/archiv/], page 22:
#*: Durch Passivrauchen steigt bei Kindern das Risiko, dass sie als Erwachsene an einer chronisch-obstruktiven Lungenerkrankung '''leiden'''.
#*:: By passive smoking, the risk increases in children that they suffer from chronic obstructive lung disease as adults.

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj-strong|leid|litt|gelitten|h|e|||a}}

